      "content": "That \"not received any credible information\" bit is still too risky. The journalist is going to see right through that if they already have a leak or a whistleblower. \n\nLook, I need you to be more aggressive in the denial. If we say something like \"We have no evidence of any unauthorized access in the last 30 days,\" it sounds like a definitive fact. It effectively kills the rumor because it's a strong, declarative statement. If we have to walk it back later, we can just say \"new evidence has come to light since our last statement,\" but for now, I need this to stop the bleeding. \n\nCan you write a version that basically functions as a flat denial of any breach occurring in that window?",
